  "body": "MIMEsniff defines things like [\"computed MIME type\"](https://mimesniff.spec.whatwg.org/#computed-mime-type) on a \"resource\", which it doesn't define. HTML mostly also refers to the computed mime type of a \"resource\", but https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/browsing-the-web.html#process-a-navigate-response uses the \"computed type of <var>response</var>\", a [response](https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-response).\r\n\r\nThis is probably not a big problem in practice.",
